# BLACKWELL UNIFIED CRYPTO ENGINE
A deterministic cryptographic architecture unifying AES‑256, ECC, and RSA
under a single governing equation.

This engine is defined by the unified transform:

C = Fθ(M, K, P)

where:
- M = message/state  
- C = ciphertext/transformed state  
- K = key material  
- P = parameters  
- θ = mode selector (aes256 | ecc | rsa | hybrid)

The architecture extends through the Blackwell Meta‑Equation:

Φ(M) — chained multi‑mode transformation  
Ψ(M) — parallel multi‑mode aggregation

